+.\" Automatically generated by Pandoc 3.10.2
+.\"
+.TH "GO\-CLEAN" "1" "August 2026" "Go 1.27" "Go programming tools and commands"
+.SH NAME
+go\-clean \- remove object files and cached files
+.SH SYNOPSIS
+\f[B]go clean\f[R] [\f[B]\-i\f[R]] [\f[B]\-r\f[R]] [\f[B]\-cache\f[R]]
+[\f[B]\-testcache\f[R]] [\f[B]\-modcache\f[R]] [\f[B]\-fuzzcache\f[R]]
+[\f[I]build flags\f[R]] [\f[I]packages\f[R]]
+.SH DESCRIPTION
+Clean removes object files from package source directories.
+The go command builds most objects in a temporary directory, so go clean
+is mainly concerned with object files left by other tools or by manual
+invocations of go build.
+.PP
+If a package argument is given or the \f[B]\-i\f[R] or \f[B]\-r\f[R]
+flag is set, clean removes the following files from each of the source
+directories corresponding to the import paths:
+.TP
+\f[B]_obj/\f[R]
+old object directory, left from Makefiles
+.TP
+\f[B]_test/\f[R]
+old test directory, left from Makefiles
+.TP
+\f[B]_testmain.go\f[R]
+old gotest file, left from Makefiles
+.TP
+\f[B]test.out\f[R]
+old test log, left from Makefiles
+.TP
+\f[B]build.out\f[R]
+old test log, left from Makefiles
+.TP
+\f[B]*.[568ao]\f[R]
+object files, left from Makefiles
+.TP
+\f[B]DIR(.exe)\f[R]
+from go build
+.TP
+\f[B]DIR.test(.exe)\f[R]
+from go test \f[B]\-c\f[R]
+.TP
+\f[B]MAINFILE(.exe)\f[R]
+from go build MAINFILE.go
+.TP
+\f[B]*.so\f[R]
+from SWIG
+.PP
+In the list, DIR represents the final path element of the directory, and
+MAINFILE is the base name of any Go source file in the directory that is
+not included when building the package.
+.SH OPTIONS
+The \f[B]\-i\f[R] flag causes clean to remove the corresponding
+installed archive or binary (what `go install' would create).
+.PP
+The \f[B]\-n\f[R] flag causes clean to print the remove commands it
+would execute, but not run them.
+.PP
+The \f[B]\-r\f[R] flag causes clean to be applied recursively to all the
+dependencies of the packages named by the import paths.
+.PP
+The \f[B]\-x\f[R] flag causes clean to print remove commands as it
+executes them.
+.PP
+The \f[B]\-cache\f[R] flag causes clean to remove the entire go build
+cache.
+.PP
+The \f[B]\-testcache\f[R] flag causes clean to expire all test results
+in the go build cache.
+.PP
+The \f[B]\-modcache\f[R] flag causes clean to remove the entire module
+download cache, including unpacked source code of versioned
+dependencies.
+.PP
+The \f[B]\-fuzzcache\f[R] flag causes clean to remove files stored in
+the Go build cache for fuzz testing.
+The fuzzing engine caches files that expand code coverage, so removing
+them may make fuzzing less effective until new inputs are found that
