+The \f[B]\-u\f[R] flag instructs get to update modules providing
+dependencies of packages named on the command line to use newer minor or
+patch releases when available.
+.PP
+The \f[B]\-u\f[R]=\f[I]patch\f[R] flag (not \f[B]\-u\f[R] patch) also
+instructs get to update dependencies, but changes the default to select
+patch releases.
+.PP
+When the \f[B]\-t\f[R] and \f[B]\-u\f[R] flags are used together, get
+will update test dependencies as well.
+.PP
+The \f[B]\-tool\f[R] flag instructs go to add a matching tool line to
+go.mod for each listed package.
+If \f[B]\-tool\f[R] is used with \(atnone, the line will be removed.
