+.\" Automatically generated by Pandoc 3.10.2
+.\"
+.TH "GO\-RUN" "1" "August 2026" "Go 1.27" "Go programming tools and commands"
+.SH NAME
+go\-run \- compile and run Go program
+.SH SYNOPSIS
+\f[B]go run\f[R] [\f[I]build flags\f[R]] [\f[B]\-exec\f[R]
+\f[I]xprog\f[R]] \f[I]package\f[R] [\f[I]arguments\&...\f[R]]
+.SH DESCRIPTION
+Run compiles and runs the named main Go package.
+Typically the package is specified as a list of .go source files from a
+single directory, but it may also be an import path, file system path,
+or pattern matching a single known package, as in `go run .' or `go run
+my/cmd'.
+.PP
+If the package argument has a version suffix (like \(atlatest or
+\(atv1.0.0), \(lqgo run\(rq builds the program in module\-aware mode,
+ignoring the go.mod file in the current directory or any parent
+directory, if there is one.
+This is useful for running programs without affecting the dependencies
+of the main module.
+.PP
+If the package argument doesn\(cqt have a version suffix, \(lqgo run\(rq
+may run in module\-aware mode or GOPATH mode, depending on the
+GO111MODULE environment variable and the presence of a go.mod file.
+See `go help modules' for details.
+If module\-aware mode is enabled, \(lqgo run\(rq runs in the context of
+the main module.
+.PP
+By default, `go run' runs the compiled binary directly: `a.out
+arguments\&...'.
+If the \f[B]\-exec\f[R] flag is given, `go run' invokes the binary using
+xprog:
+.RS
+.PP
+`xprog a.out arguments\&...'.
+.RE
+.PP
+If the \f[B]\-exec\f[R] flag is not given, GOOS or GOARCH is different
+from the system default, and a program named
+go_\f[I]G\f[R]\f[I]O\f[R]\f[I]O\f[R]\f[I]S\f[R]_GOARCH_exec can be found
+on the current search path, `go run' invokes the binary using that
+program, for example `go_js_wasm_exec a.out arguments\&...'.
+This allows execution of cross\-compiled programs when a simulator or
+other execution method is available.
+.PP
+By default, `go run' compiles the binary without generating the
+information used by debuggers, to reduce build time.
+To include debugger information in the binary, use `go build'.
+.PP
+The go command places \f[I]$GOROOT/bin\f[R] at the beginning of $PATH in
+the subprocess environment, so that subprocesses that execute `go'
+commands use the same `go' as their parent.
+.PP
+The exit status of Run is not the exit status of the compiled binary.
+.PP
+For more about build flags, see `go help build'.
+For more about specifying packages, see `go help packages'.
+.SH SEE ALSO
+\f[B]go build\f[R](1).
+.SH AUTHOR
+This manual page was created using help2man and afterwards updating the
+output.
+It is maintained by the Debian Go Compiler Team
+<team+go\-compiler\(attracker.debian.org> for the Debian project (and
+may be used by others).
