+.SH NAME
+go\-vet \- report likely mistakes in packages
+.SH SEE ALSO
+\f[B]go vet\f[R] [\f[I]build flags\f[R]] [\f[B]\-vettool\f[R]
+\f[I]prog\f[R]] [\f[I]vet flags\f[R]] [\f[I]packages\f[R]]
+.SH DESCRIPTION
+Vet runs the Go vet tool (cmd/vet) on the named packages and reports
+diagnostics.
+.SH OPTIONS
+It supports these flags:
+.PP
+\f[B]\-c\f[R] \f[I]int\f[R]
+.RS
+.PP
+display offending line with this many lines of context (default
+\f[B]\-1\f[R])
+.RE
+.PP
+\f[B]\-json\f[R]
+.RS
+.PP
+emit JSON output
+.RE
+.PP
+\f[B]\-fix\f[R]
+.RS
+.PP
+instead of printing each diagnostic, apply its first fix (if any)
+.RE
+.PP
+\f[B]\-diff\f[R]
+.RS
+.PP
+instead of applying each fix, print the patch as a unified diff
+.RE
+.PP
+The \f[B]\-vettool\f[R]=\f[I]prog\f[R] flag selects a different analysis
+tool with alternative or additional checks.
+For example, the `shadow' analyzer can be built and run using these
+commands:
+.IP
+.EX
+go install golang.org/x/tools/go/analysis/passes/shadow/cmd/shadow\(atlatest
+go vet \-vettool=$(which shadow)
+.EE
+.PP
+Alternative vet tools should be built atop
+golang.org/x/tools/go/analysis/unitchecker, which handles the
+interaction with go vet.
+.PP
+The default vet tool is `go tool vet' or cmd/vet.
+For help on its checkers and their flags, run `go tool vet help'.
+For details of a specific checker such as `printf', see `go tool vet
+help printf'.
+.PP
+For more about specifying packages, see `go help packages'.
+.PP
+The build flags supported by go vet are those that control package
+resolution and execution, such as \f[B]\-C\f[R], \f[B]\-n\f[R],
+\f[B]\-x\f[R], \f[B]\-v\f[R], \f[B]\-tags\f[R], and
+\f[B]\-toolexec\f[R].
+For more about these flags, see `go help build'.
+.SH SEE ALSO
+\f[B]go fmt\f[R](1), \f[B]go fix\f[R](1).
+.SH AUTHOR
+This manual page was created using help2man and afterwards updating the
+output.
+It is maintained by the Debian Go Compiler Team
+<team+go\-compiler\(attracker.debian.org> for the Debian project (and
+may be used by others).
