+.\" Automatically generated by Pandoc 3.10.2
+.\"
+.TH "GOFMT" "1" "August 2026" "Go 1.27" "Go programming tools and commands"
+.SH NAME
+gofmt \- format Go programs
+.SH SYNOPSIS
+\f[B]gofmt\f[R] [\f[I]flags\f[R]] [\f[I]path \&...\f[R]]
+.SH DESCRIPTION
+Gofmt formats Go programs.
+It uses tabs for indentation and blanks for alignment.
+Alignment assumes that an editor is using a fixed\-width font.
+.PP
+Without an explicit path, it processes the standard input.
+Given a file, it operates on that file; given a directory, it operates
+on all .go files in that directory, recursively.
+(Files starting with a period are ignored.)
+By default, gofmt prints the reformatted sources to standard output.
+.SH OPTIONS
+.TP
+\f[B]\-cpuprofile\f[R] \f[I]string\f[R]
+write cpu profile to this file
+.TP
+\f[B]\-d\f[R]
+display diffs instead of rewriting files
+.TP
+\f[B]\-e\f[R]
+report all errors (not just the first 10 on different lines)
+.TP
+\f[B]\-l\f[R]
+list files whose formatting differs from gofmt\(cqs
+.TP
+\f[B]\-r\f[R] \f[I]string\f[R]
+rewrite rule (e.g., `a[b:len(a)] \-> a[b:]')
+.TP
+\f[B]\-s\f[R]
+simplify code
+.TP
+\f[B]\-w\f[R]
+write result to (source) file instead of stdout
